---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Chat from '../components/Chat.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About Paperhint — School Software Built with Teachers"
  description="Why we built Paperhint: school software that makes a school faster, with an assistant at every desk so the hours go to teaching."
  canonical="https://paperhint.com/about"
>
<Nav />

<header class="page-hero">
  <!-- gratitude ribbon: same engine as home, its own words and pace -->
  <div class="hero-ribbon" data-speed="34" data-drop="420" style="--band:#FF8A3D;--band-echo:var(--yellow);--band-text:#10201A;--band-kw:#FFFFFF"
       data-words="*Thank* *you* to the teachers, the staff rooms and the last bell · to *report* *cards* written by hand · to the *schools* *that* *raised* *us* · this one is for the *evenings* we owe you ·"
       aria-hidden="true">
    <svg preserveAspectRatio="none" focusable="false">
      <path class="ribbon-echo"/>
      <path class="ribbon-line"/>
      <path class="bowl-line" id="about-band" fill="none" stroke="none"/>
      <text class="bowl-marquee"><textPath href="#about-band" data-speed="34"></textPath></text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap hero-content">
    <span class="tagline"><span class="tag">ABOUT</span> Note from the founders <i>·</i></span>
    <h1 class="display">Why <em>w</em>e built this</h1>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section-pad" style="padding-top:26px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="letter reveal">
      <div class="cr-gang-solo" aria-hidden="true">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/assets/img/stickers/classroom-gang.webp" type="image/webp">
          <img src="/assets/img/stickers/classroom-gang.png" alt="" width="1100" height="608">
        </picture>
      </div>
      <p>Dear schools that raised us,</p>

      <p>We were your students once. We sat in your classrooms, lined up in your
      corridors, and carried home the report cards you wrote by hand. Long
      before Paperhint was an idea, you were already doing the work &mdash;
      quietly, year after year.</p>

      <p>And because we were there, we saw what it cost. We watched our teachers
      stay back after the last bell to redraw a timetable someone's absence had
      broken. We saw marks copied from register to register until midnight, notes
      photocopied until the ink gave out, and principals holding entire academic
      years together with little more than patience and a filing cabinet. Years
      later we came back as visitors, and nothing had changed &mdash; the same
      invisible work, still carried by hand.</p>

      <p>Somewhere in those visits the thought took hold: the people who gave us
      everything were spending their evenings on work no one ever thanked them
      for. We wanted to give something back &mdash; not a tribute, but time.
      That is when this idea found us.</p>

      <p>Paperhint is our way of returning what you spent on us. The answer
      sheets that mark themselves against your rubric, the question paper
      drafted in minutes for your syllabus, the parent who hears about homework
      the moment it's assigned &mdash;
      every one of these is an evening handed back to someone who once handed
      theirs to us.</p>

      <p>If your school still runs on the invisible machine, let us show you the
      same term running on one page. It would be an honour.</p>

      <p class="letter-sign">&mdash; with gratitude, the Paperhint team</p>
      <span class="fold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <!-- Founder: refine freely — this is drafted from your telling of the story -->
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div data-component="cta-banner"></div>
  </div>
</section>


<Footer />
<Chat />
<div class="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
</Base>
